    "title": "Senator John Cornyn addresses gun rights and government shutdown in recent posts - Houston Republic",
    "text": "Senator John Cornyn, a Republican from Texas, shared a series of posts on his X (formerly Twitter) account on October 7 and 8, 2025, addressing issues related to gun rights, the ongoing government shutdown, and U.S.-China relations.\nOn October 7, Cornyn highlighted his meeting with National Shooting Sports Foundation (NSSF) leaders, stating, “Great to speak with @NSSF President Joe Bartozzi, SVP Larry Keane, & other members about defending our 2nd Amendment rights & the Protection of Lawful Commerce in Arms Act, which I cosponsored to protect firearm manufactures, distributors, & dealers from being held liable when https://t.co/hZQItWc42e”.\nLater the same day, Cornyn commented on the government shutdown and its impact on military pay. He quoted GOP House Speaker Mike Johnson, writing, “GOP leaders are upping pressure on Democrats to end the shutdown ahead of next week’s troop pay deadline. ‘You have to get it resolved by Oct. 13, which is Monday, in order to process those checks,’ Mike Johnson just said. @politico”.\nOn October 8, Cornyn referenced a Wall Street Journal opinion piece regarding U.S.-China relations, posting, “The Oct. 7 Warning for the U.S. on China by @RepGallagher https://t.co/mMH49EX5NH via @WSJopinion”.\nSenator Cornyn has served in the U.S. Senate since 2002, having won re-election in multiple general elections: defeating Ron Kirk in 2002 with 55% of the vote, Rick Noriega in 2008 with 54.8%, David Alameel in 2014 with 61.6%, and MJ Hegar in 2020 with 53.5%.",
